  "body": "**Stacked on #540** (base branch `stack/pr540-base` = #540 head `acc19170`). Once #540 lands, this PR retargets to `main`. It adds one directory, `research/lean-pending-derivation/`. **No #540 file is changed**, so #540's hashed manifests and receipts stay valid.\n\n## What it closes\n#540's `PhysicalSourceConnection.pendingTag` supplies the pending ranges `[15,22)` and `[1,29)` by hand. Its README notes that \"neither Lean nor the source-extraction check binds these ranges to the source schedule\". #1228 derived them in Python. This PR does the derivation in Lean 4.21 and proves it equal to #540's actual definition.\n\n## Theorems\nAll are proved by `decide`, using only `propext` and `Quot.sound` (some use no axioms).\n- `PendingDerivation.idle_ranks_and_nesting`: for all 10 idle events, levels nest and the derived pending size equals the scheduled rank.\n- `pending_child1 / pending_child2`: `[15..21]` and `[1..28]`.\n- `hosted_windows`: for all 16 tags, stage 2 is in the child's window, the host pair is not pair 0, and `offset+width \u2264 |pending|`.\n- `target_derived`: every extracted `targetMask` is exactly the `[offset, offset+width)` slice of the derived pending axes. This also checks the extractor's hard-coded bases.\n- `PendingBinding.pendingTag_derived` and `pending_eq_derived`: #540's `pendingTag` and `pending` equal the derived masks.\n- `PendingBinding.selected_invocation_completion_derived`: #540's completion theorem, restated with the derived mask.\n\nDefinitions: L\u208b\u2081 = {0}, L_\u2113 = [0,8) \u222a E\u2081 \u222a \u2026 \u222a E_\u2113 (E_s = exterior axes of the stage-s route), pending = L_target \\ L_source, and windows follow PR442's last-touch rule. The schedule and blocks are a Python-extracted literal (`generate_pending_schedule.py --check`, byte-exact against #540's pinned inputs). This is the same trust boundary as #540's other literals.\n\nSix mutation controls each fail because `decide` refutes the mutated statement:\n- L\u208b\u2081 empty;\n- L\u208b\u2081 set to the whole local block;\n- exterior blocks off by one stage;\n- the first two blocks swapped;\n- child 1 advanced before the selected call;\n- child 1 claimed on the previous block.\n\n## Not covered\n- The level model is a definition. Its agreement with the PR386 frames (L\u208b\u2081 = span(q) in the `B_port \u2295 I\u2085\u2086` chart) is not proved. It is constrained only by ranks, nesting and the extracted target masks.\n- Ascending axis order within a child is the offset convention shared with #540's extractor.\n- Only one invocation is covered. No cost, all-size or \u03ba claim.\n\n## Reproduce\n```sh\ncd research/lean-multi-host-source && lake exe cache get <the five Mathlib modules in BUILD.md>\nlake build PhysicalSourceConnection     # 3m24s measured on Apple silicon with the Mathlib cache\ncd ../.. && python3 research/lean-pending-derivation/verify.py   # ~17 s, prints PASS_PR540_PENDING_RANGES_DERIVED_IN_LEAN\n```\n`verify.py` runs the generator check, compiles the three modules against #540's build through `lake env`, audits the axioms of all seven theorems and runs the controls.\n\n**Credit:** the Lean formalization, ownership literals and gap identification are cheesegrader's #540. Construction and hosting are from #434/#442, and the bit geometry is from PR386. The Python predecessor is #1228. Prepared by Douglas Colkitt with substantial Claude (Anthropic) assistance. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
